From: cheebun <cheebun@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: drop PON paths from the PPE offload rework

This tree does not carry the AN7581 PON data path (922), its PPE
metadata (925), the legacy xPON compatibility layer (920-20) or the
PON-only PPPoE MTU accounting (920-17). 9995 and 9996 were written on
top of them, so remove what only makes sense with a PON GDM device:

- airoha_ppe_pon_lookup_tag()/airoha_ppe_pon_select_flow() and the
  egress_dev out parameter of airoha_ppe_foe_entry_prepare().
- The PPPoE redirect to a PON GDM device in
  airoha_ppe_flow_offload_replace(); on an Ethernet PPPoE WAN the
  forward path already resolves the ppp device to the GDM netdev.
- The pon_mapping and ppp_uplink drop reasons.
- The CONFIG_AIROHA_PON_COMPAT multicast provider.

QinQ/VPM handling, aging, drop accounting for the remaining reasons,
the debugfs summary/config/bind_rate files and the QDMA/NPU debugfs
state are kept unchanged.

